WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.170
Originally this land was council-owned, but
at the time it was proposed for forestry.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:14.680
At the time, the community got together and
said, we'd prefer it to be a native reserve,

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.090
so since then we've been developing it partnership
with a group of residents.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.310
We have the Silverstream Reserve Advisory
group, we've had a fair amount of input from

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:22.660
ECAN as well.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.750
We've also had massive support from Mainpower,
so they've been attending all of the planting

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.869
days we do, which is really cool, they always
have a presence and they're really interested

00:00:29.869 --> 00:00:30.869
in what we're doing.

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:35.760
We're squeezing it to make sure that we can
pull all the soil out when we pull it.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.710
Clarkville School they're great, they come
down here on a regular basis and plant and

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.400
it's amazing how quick they can get things
done.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.200
We're just putting on a combi-guard.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.800
It keeps out the weeds.

00:00:53.809 --> 00:00:55.730
They love coming down to Silverstream.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:58.890
I'm sure part of the appeal is working with
Dan.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:01.620
You guys set that up okay, you guys run that.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:07.060
A group of kids made up that they were going
to be part of a dirt factory and they had

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.280
a little chain of workers going, and doing
different jobs.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:13.940
Today they were like, "Can we do that again?",
and we're were like, "Yeah sure, it's not

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.780
dirt this time, it's mulch," So yeah, they
love it.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.440
You embrace the chaos, basically I just say
my bit at the start, I just say right, plants

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.430
are here, tools are here, let's go for it.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:27.430
And then look what we've got now.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:32.060
We've got a bunch of them doing the mulch
delivery, some of them doing watering,

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:37.640
others are going around and making sure the
guards are fitted properly and things like

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.470
that, so you get this sort of teamwork, and
then you get these really cool initiatives

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.830
coming through.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:45.280
So yeah, you can see the future leaders coming
through in that regard as well.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:51.500
The community, the ones who we see coming
through here are so thrilled to see it being

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.480
developed and how things are growing so well,

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:59.980
so we get quite a bit of feedback from people now and it's really good. So we're all enthusiastic.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.380
It's great, it's beneficial.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:05.040
I mean we come here on walks, the kids can
see what they've done.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.470
Yeah, it's making the place look way better.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:13.400
This ground is pretty stony and weedy and
scrubby, so by the end of it, it will be great,

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.840
it will look fantastic.

